! Face-centred-cubic hydrogen at 6.5 bohr: an itinerant ferromagnet cheap
! enough to converge the transverse spin susceptibility on, and the cell the
! P63 identities are measured on.
!
! Three things about it are deliberate.
!
!   * fcc rather than a chain. The kernel of the transverse channel is
!     B_xc(r)/m(r), which grows without bound as the density falls, so a cell
!     with vacuum has an enormous kernel where there is nothing to respond: on
!     a hydrogen chain with 8 bohr between images |B_xc/m| reaches 173 in the
!     tail against 21 in the core, and the leading eigenvalue of X_0 F moves
!     from 1.13 to 0.92 as the density clip moves from 1e-6 to 1e-2. A compact
!     cell has a density ratio of 29 rather than 1858 and the same eigenvalue
!     is stable to the clip.
!   * nosym and noinv with the whole 4x4x4 grid. The states at k + q are read
!     out of this same grid, which needs it closed under translation by q, and
!     X_0(G, G') is a matrix in two G indices that nothing here symmetrises.
!   * a = 6.5 bohr. Below about 6 the cell is not magnetic at all and above it
!     the density ratio climbs; here the moment is 0.53 mu_B, which is an
!     itinerant ferromagnet rather than a set of local moments.
!   * starting_magnetization = 0.9 and NOT 1.0, which is the third deliberate
!     thing and the one that used to be wrong. See below.
!
! **The seed decides which solution this cell converges to, and 1.0 picks the
! wrong one.** Hydrogen has one valence electron, so a starting magnetization of
! 1.0 is a *fully polarized* atom: the minority channel starts at exactly zero
! and the first potential is built at |zeta| = 1, which is the saturated point
! every clamp in defumat/xc is about (CLAUDE.md's clamp-tangent trap). From
! there the run leaves the ferromagnetic branch altogether. Measured, same cell,
! same everything else, conv_thr = 1e-10:
!
!     seed   converged   iterations       E (Ry)          m        vs. nonmagnetic
!     1.0       yes         126        -0.9845889092    0.02728       -0.13 meV
!     0.9       yes           7        -0.9802841602    0.53125      +58.44 meV
!     0.0       yes           6        -0.9845791913    0.00000            --
!
! Both are genuine converged solutions of the same functional; they are not the
! same state, and the one this cell is FOR is the second. A run seeded at 1.0
! reaches a barely-magnetic solution whose Goldstone residual is 0.40 against a
! tolerance of 0.02, which is not a defect in the susceptibility -- there is
! almost no moment for a spin wave to be a rotation OF. That is what four of
! test_magnons.py's eight tests were reporting (OPEN.md Part V).
!
! **The ferromagnetic solution is not the ground state and that is why the cell
! is here.** It converges at m = 0.53 mu_B and sits 58 meV *above* the
! nonmagnetic solution of the same input, and the transverse susceptibility says
! so: its leading eigenvalue exceeds one at q = (0, 0, 1/4), which means the
! uniform state is unstable against an infinitesimal spiral of that pitch. That
! prediction is now confirmed by a route sharing no machinery with it: the
! spin-spiral scan of h-fcc-spiral-scan.in, seeded the same way, has its minimum
! at exactly q = (0, 0, 1/4), 150 meV below the ferromagnet.
!
! No lattice constant fixes the instability -- at 7.0 bohr the ferromagnet is
! 7.22 meV below the nonmagnetic solution and still soft at finite q, at 8.0 it
! is 73.80 meV below at m = 0.97 and still soft (both at the saturated seed,
! which is the branch those two land on there) -- because a half-filled band on
! any lattice prefers antiferromagnetic order. So this cell is the *identities*
! case (Goldstone, periodicity, the q -> -q reflection), and fcc nickel is the
! physics one. See PLAN.md P63.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 6.5,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.01,
    nspin = 2
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.9
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 0 0 0
